<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24141" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intentātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		intento, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a stretching out</i> or <i>extending
				towards</i> a thing. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oculi ad intentationem subitam digitorum
					comprimuntur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ira, 2, 4, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a reproaching</i>
			with a thing: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">criminum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 46</span></i>
			 dub. (al. intentio).</div>
